---
title: Harissa Rice
description: Harissa-infused rice where the paste sautés with the rice before steaming, resulting in a deeply seasoned, savory side dish with a rich colour.
image: https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F71bc7670-a4f2-4716-a92a-a5943ae3b594_6000x4000.jpeg
source: https://veganscratchkitchen.substack.com/p/weeknight-dinner-lemon-pepper-tofu
author: Vegan Scratch Kitchen
tags: rice, side, vegan, harissa, gluten-free, middle-eastern-inspired, quick
servings: 2
prep time: 5 minutes
cook time: 30 minutes
time required: 35 minutes
---

Place a #medium sauce pot{} over medium heat and allow to warm for ~{2-3%minutes}.

Add @avocado oil{2%tbsp} and allow to warm for ~{15-20%seconds}. Add @long grain white rice{1%cup}(rinsed and dried in a strainer ahead of time) with a few pinches of @salt{} and stir to coat evenly in the oil.

Add @harissa paste{3%tbsp} with another pinch of @salt{} and stir to combine with the rice. Cook for ~{2-3%minutes}.

Pour in @water{1¾%cups} with another pinch of @salt{}. Bring to a boil, then cover with a lid and reduce heat to a low simmer. Cook for ~{30%minutes}.
